en.use:
Use to calculate the ELTS score and assess the corresponding risk group in patients with chronic myeloid leukemia. 

The formula used to calculate the score requires continuous variables:

age: patient age in years;

spleen size below costal margin: measured in cm;

peripheral blood blasts: measured as a percentage;

platelet count: measured in 10^9/l.

The formula calculates the score as: 0.0025 * (age / 10)^3 + 0.0615 * spleen size + 0.1052 * blasts + 0.4104 * (platelet count / 1000)^-0.5. 

The score is then mapped to a risk group:

low risk: score ≤ 1.5626;

intermediate risk: score > 1.5626 and ≤ 2.2185;

high risk: score > 2.2185.
